course: dictionary
lesson: 6023
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. The context tells you which meaning the writer intends. Medusa is a good example, because it is a name in a myth and also a word from science.
explain: «Greek myths tell of heroes like Heracles with his twelve labours, Perseus and Medusa, and Theseus and the Minotaur.» Here Medusa is a name. The capital letter, the word myths, and the heroes all tell you it is a character from an old story.
explain: In a science lesson about the sea, medusa means something different: the swimming, umbrella-shaped stage of a jellyfish. Ask yourself which topic you are reading about. Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Medusa is a name in Greek myth: a monster, a Gorgon, with snakes for hair.
fact: Anyone who looked at Medusa's face was turned to stone. The hero Perseus defeated her by looking at her reflection in his shiny shield.
fact: In science, a medusa is the swimming, umbrella-shaped stage of a jellyfish or similar sea creature.
fact: The plural of medusa in science can be medusae or medusas.
fact: A capital letter at the start of a name often shows that it is a person, place or character.
exercise: «Greek myths tell of heroes like Heracles, Perseus and Medusa.» In this sentence, what is Medusa? | *A character from an old story | A jelly swimming in the sea | A kind of shield | A school subject
exercise: Lia reads: «The medusa drifted slowly past the boat.» In a lesson about the sea, what does medusa mean? | *The swimming, umbrella-shaped stage of a jellyfish | A stone statue | A monster with snakes for hair
exercise: Which word tells you that the sentence is about stories from long ago? | *Myths | Tennis | Yesterday | Puddles
test: In science, what is a medusa? | A shiny shield | *The swimming, umbrella-shaped stage of a jellyfish | A Gorgon with snakes for hair | A type of rock
test: Which sentence uses Medusa as a name from a myth? | The medusae were floating near the rocks. | The jellyfish had a polyp stage. | *Perseus cut off Medusa's head. | The medusa swam past the boat.
exam: Mia reads: «Perseus looked at Medusa's reflection in his shield.» Why did he not look straight at her face? | *Because anyone who looked at her face was turned to stone | Because the shield was too heavy to lift | Because her reflection was too small to see | Because she was asleep
